<https://purl.org/oquo-huron#LexicallySuggestLogicallyDefineIssue>
        a                       owl:Class ;
        rdfs:label              "lexically suggest logically define issue" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf         oquo:IssueByNonConformity ;
        skos:definition         "The name of the class A is exhibited by class B, but they are not semantically related." ;
        oquo:hasRecommendation  "The information that can be inferred from the name must be formalized as logical axioms in the ontology. In other words, the human readable content and the machine readable content should be aligned. For example, the class 'juvenile osteochondrosis of foot' should be semantically related to the 'osteochondrosis' and 'foot' ontology classes, if these exist." .

